    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, who pace our roster with efficiency scores of 81.88 and 75.27, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite park factor and a favorable matchup against Will Warren, where his dynamic platoon advantage creates a massive wedge in his expected production. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-output game against Stock; despite the elite catcher arm behind the plate potentially curbing aggressive base-running, the combination of SP skill and a favorable wind-out forecast makes him a must-start staple. **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** also command attention, both hovering near the 71-74 range, largely due to their ability to exploit Kyle Freeland\u2019s struggles with left-handed contact, keeping our offensive floor exceptionally high.\n\nThe deepest decision on the bench centered on **Dominic Smith**, who finished with a respectable score of 51.37. While **Dominic Smith** held a solid platoon advantage against Bradley, the optimizer ultimately pivoted toward the defensive and positional versatility of **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** to maintain our roster balance. Our primary risk remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Jacob Wilson**. While we have projected them into the spots reflected in their strong efficiency scores, any late-scratch adjustments or lineup shuffling could force a pivot to avoid sinking our game cap efficiency. We are monitoring **Sam Antonacci** closely as well; his 61.82 score is buoyed heavily by his projected leadoff spot, making him a critical engine for Runs today if he holds that premium position against Holmes.",
